  {
    "sha": "f55eeaa49dbe47cda0ecd702255765d2f9025f0d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGY1NWVlYWE0OWRiZTQ3Y2RhMGVjZDcwMjI1NTc2NWQyZjkwMjVmMGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T19:29:07Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T19:29:07Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gate): skip the #1950 known-fail heavy tests at the cut, check they still fail\n\nThe v0.24.0 cut gate (run 44362577581) was red on three #[ignore]d tests\nthat pin the open, blocked issue #1950. They were added red on purpose and\nno merge of this cycle made them fail. The output is the announced\nOffset-rings fallback: no lost pass, no missing level, no gouge.\n\n- xtask/src/known_fail.rs lists the three tests. Their heavy lanes skip\n  them by name (--exact --skip) and the plan prints\n  \"SKIPPED (known fail, #1950): <test>\".\n- Each skipped test gets its own release step that is ok only when the\n  test fails. A pass or a renamed test fails the gate.\n- The release tier reads each pinned issue with gh. A closed issue fails\n  the gate; an unreadable state prints a note.\n- The decision is in RECOMMENDED.md under v0.24.0; #1950 is a Known\n  issues note in RELEASE_NOTES.md.\n- Review notes: four decision headings use ##.\n\nRefs #1950\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
