  {
    "sha": "9dfe7dff18834bca8a59f85b9324efb98103a974",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDlkZmU3ZGZmMTg4MzRiY2E4YTU5Zjg1YjkzMjRlZmI5ODEwM2E5NzQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T19:35:41Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T19:35:41Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gate): a known-fail step needs its own test FAILED; gh reads upstream with a limit\n\nReview of f55eeaa49:\n- expect_fail_note is ok only when the read_log note is `failed: ...` and\n  its [tests: ...] list names the expected test exactly. A crash of the\n  test binary (exit 101 / -1 with no `test ... FAILED` line), a compile\n  error, another failed test or a pass is a FAIL. Step.expect_fail now\n  carries the test name.\n- gh issue view uses -R NeoTech/Camcraft and a 30 s limit. The decision\n  text says that the cut job has no GH_TOKEN, so on the runner the issue\n  check prints a note and the known-fail steps are the guard.\n- heavy_tests pins that a lane without a known-fail entry has nothing\n  between --test-threads and --ignored.\n- RELEASE_NOTES.md: two open defects have a workaround (#2561, #1950).\n\nThe previous commit also changed four unrelated decision headings in\nRECOMMENDED.md from `#` to `##` (#870, #1186, #2019, #2464), a review note\nof PR #2564.\n\nRefs #1950\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
