  {
    "sha": "d7c897ae473478f973b5a0b112ee196a0270be89",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGQ3Yzg5N2FlNDczNDc4Zjk3M2I1YTBiMTEyZWUxOTZhMDI3MGJlODk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T19:39:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T19:39:53Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gate): a known-fail step needs the test's own #1950 assert, not any failure\n\nDelta review of 9dfe7dff1: a FAILED of the right test for another reason\n(a planner panic, a gouge or collision warning, another assert) read as\n\"red as expected\". Each KNOWN_FAIL entry now names the test file, the\npinned assert in the test body and a stable piece of its message. The\nstep is ok only when the test's own panic block is `panicked at <file>`\nand holds that text; otherwise it is \"KNOWN FAIL, DIFFERENT REASON\".\n\n- motion reaches_the_air_planner: \"hops \" (the HOP_BUDGET assert)\n- motion plans_adaptive: \" right: Adaptive\" (the strategy assert_eq)\n- app whole_model: \"every level keeps the HSM plan\"\n\nknown_fail_tests pins that each assert is in its test body and that the\nreason comes from it, with unit cases for another assert, another file,\nanother thread and an empty log. The decision text says so.\n\nRefs #1950\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
